---
// The headline is the diagram: each role sits inside its own sentence.
const workers = ["W1", "W2", "W3"];
---

<section id="architecture" class="sec roles">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="roles-type" aria-label="One plans. Three build. One checks.">
      <span class="rl rv" aria-hidden="true">
        One
        <span class="chip chip-o">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100">
            <path d="M50 6 C53 36 64 47 94 50 C64 53 53 64 50 94 C47 64 36 53 6 50 C36 47 47 36 50 6 Z" />
          </svg>
          Orchestrator
        </span>
        plans.
      </span>
      <span class="rl rv rv2" aria-hidden="true">
        Three
        <span class="chip chip-w">
          <span class="avs">
            {workers.map((w, i) => (
              <b class={`av-${i}`}>{w}</b>
            ))}
          </span>
          Workers
        </span>
        build.
      </span>
      <span class="rl rv rv3" aria-hidden="true">
        One
        <span class="chip chip-s">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100">
            <path d="M6 50 C22 24 36 16 50 16 C64 16 78 24 94 50 C78 76 64 84 50 84 C36 84 22 76 6 50 Z" class="lid" />
            <circle cx="50" cy="50" r="15" />
          </svg>
          Supervisor
        </span>
        checks.
      </span>
    </h2>
    <p class="roles-note rv">
      The orchestrator writes each worker a short brief. Workers build in parallel. The supervisor reads the result and
      never edits a file.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
